nio: call bsdinit_task directly again; the deferred AST never fires

Runs 607 through 612 deferred bsdinit_task() to the init thread's bsd_ast
and every photo stopped at "defer bsdinit_task to init thread AST".  The
init thread is created (UT post-cloneproc / post-procfind appear) but is
never scheduled early enough to take an AST, so the call never happens and
exec /sbin/launchd is never reached.

The only path that ever reached exec was the direct call: runs 603-605
showed load_init_program / exec marks when bsdinit_task() was called at
the end of bsd_init().  load_init_program now also switches to initproc's
map (the 217 patch), so restore that direct call.  A distinct panel mark
confirms this round took this path.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
@@ -1226,6 +1226,8 @@ bsd_init(void)
 	 * reached), so let the normal bsd_ast() trigger run bsdinit_task() on the
 	 * real init thread, where current_proc/task/map are all correct. */
-	nio_bmark("\nnio: defer bsdinit_task to init thread AST");
+	/* nio: the deferred AST never fires on this board (607..612); call it. */
+	nio_bmark("\nnio: call bsdinit_task directly (613)");
+	bsdinit_task();
 }
 
 #if defined(XNU_OWNER_ROOT_AUDIT) && XNU_OWNER_ROOT_AUDIT
